{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a parokhet.</b> Thus we find that Solomon made one for the entrance of the Devir. Perhaps the wall was wood, because he mentioned that the entire measure of the House was sixty. And Rashi z\"l explained that forty was the Hekhal and twenty the Devir, and silver sockets because of the honor of the Ark. Now the Devir was double the place of the Holy of Holies in length, in breadth, and in height. And do not be astonished because it is written that the height of the House was thirty cubits, and the Devir a third of the House, because there were upper chambers above the Kapporet, which is the Devir, and it is written in Chronicles: and the upper chambers overlaid with gold (2 Chronicles 3:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The comment on 'the Devir was double the place of the Holy of Holies' is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally as it stands. The reference to 'silver sockets' appears to draw from 1 Kings 6–7 rather than the Exodus passage."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:40.276681498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}